# 07 — Geometry Tools

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/06-more-shapes` first (the footprint refactor, cylinders, free-forms, lines, point editing, and its notes for the next session). The idea came from `plans/thinking-02-tweaking-shapes`. This is the last geometry phase; semantics and prefabs move to 08. It adds:
> - **wall thickness** per room, with the walls now grown **inward** from the outline;
> - **taper** and **bevel** on volumes: a box becomes a pyramid, a tall cylinder gets a rounded top;
> - **tilt** (`pitch` and `roll`) on boxes and cylinders, with gizmo rings, so a cylinder can lie on its side;
> - **holes**, a third kind next to room and volume: any closed shape can be one, and it cuts the shapes in its own group and its sibling groups;
> - **ramps**, a new shape type: a path with a width, smooth or stepped (stairs), straight, curved or spiral.
>
> Everything is still shapes: a door is a box hole in the room's group, not an anchored entity. The groundwork comes first (07.1): every shape reduces to a closed triangle mesh, and rendering, picking and the marquee run from it, because none of the new shapes is a vertical prism anymore. The agent gets all of it through `draw_shapes` and `update_nodes`, with no new tools. The work is split into small increments (§10). Each one ends with the human ↔ agent loop still working and a browser checklist for Orlando. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 07") as they land. Log progress in a §13 at the end of this file, as 06 did.

